WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.890 --> 00:00:06.750
The Economist Intelligence
Unit Democracy Index

00:00:06.750 --> 00:00:08.941
seeks to measure the health of democracy

00:00:08.941 --> 00:00:12.010
in pretty much all the
countries around the world.

00:00:12.010 --> 00:00:14.210
It breaks this down into five categories.

00:00:14.210 --> 00:00:17.300
The electoral process, the
functioning of government,

00:00:17.300 --> 00:00:20.460
civil liberties, political participation,

00:00:20.460 --> 00:00:21.970
and political culture.

00:00:21.970 --> 00:00:23.300
The scores range from Norway

00:00:23.300 --> 00:00:26.200
which we rate as the most
democratic country on Earth

00:00:26.200 --> 00:00:28.080
all the way down to North Korea,

00:00:28.080 --> 00:00:30.200
a hereditary communist monarchy

00:00:30.200 --> 00:00:31.850
which is by far the least.

00:00:31.850 --> 00:00:33.120
Although the world has obviously gotten

00:00:33.120 --> 00:00:34.630
a lot more democratic

00:00:34.630 --> 00:00:37.190
over the past century
and the past 30 years

00:00:37.190 --> 00:00:39.160
since the end of the Cold War

00:00:39.160 --> 00:00:41.340
but since the EIU started measuring it

00:00:41.340 --> 00:00:45.203
which was in 2006, things appear
to have regressed somewhat.

00:00:50.000 --> 00:00:52.180
Today roughly half the world's people live

00:00:52.180 --> 00:00:54.040
in some form of democracy

00:00:54.040 --> 00:00:56.030
but by our rather strict measurements,

00:00:56.030 --> 00:01:00.600
only about 5% live in what
we call a full democracy

00:01:00.600 --> 00:01:04.920
and a good third or so live
in solid authoritarian regimes

00:01:04.920 --> 00:01:07.110
with a big portion of that in China.

00:01:07.110 --> 00:01:08.530
One of the less gloomy findings

00:01:08.530 --> 00:01:11.890
is that political
participation seems to be up.

00:01:11.890 --> 00:01:13.620
This is probably related

00:01:13.620 --> 00:01:16.390
to a widespread feeling
in a lot of countries

00:01:16.390 --> 00:01:18.310
that democracy's under threat,

00:01:18.310 --> 00:01:20.290
that the threats of fake news,

00:01:20.290 --> 00:01:22.070
subversion by foreign powers

00:01:22.070 --> 00:01:25.760
such as Russia and the rise
of authoritarian leaders

00:01:25.760 --> 00:01:28.110
from Hungary to Poland

00:01:28.110 --> 00:01:30.400
to all kinds of places

00:01:30.400 --> 00:01:32.890
means that people can't take
democracy for granted anymore

00:01:32.890 --> 00:01:35.050
and so, you'll see a lot
more people demonstrating

00:01:35.050 --> 00:01:39.373
in the streets, getting out
to vote and organizing online.

00:01:43.990 --> 00:01:45.160
The most improved indicator

00:01:45.160 --> 00:01:48.050
was to do with women's
participation in politics.

00:01:48.050 --> 00:01:51.220
Partly that reflects a genuine improvement

00:01:51.220 --> 00:01:52.450
in the status of women

00:01:52.450 --> 00:01:54.450
and the increased likelihood

00:01:54.450 --> 00:01:56.820
that voters are prepared to vote for them.

00:01:56.820 --> 00:01:58.760
Alas it also represents a certain amount

00:01:58.760 --> 00:02:00.390
of gaming the system particularly

00:02:00.390 --> 00:02:02.270
by authoritarian regimes,

00:02:02.270 --> 00:02:05.950
Rwanda, for example, has a
majority female parliament

00:02:05.950 --> 00:02:07.610
which sounds great until you realize

00:02:07.610 --> 00:02:09.710
that the parliament
has no power whatsoever

00:02:09.710 --> 00:02:12.410
and the president is very much male.

00:02:12.410 --> 00:02:13.930
It might seem like a paradox

00:02:13.930 --> 00:02:16.840
that even as democracy
retreats around the world,

00:02:16.840 --> 00:02:18.708
political participation has gone up

00:02:18.708 --> 00:02:21.440
but it's not, it's a
reaction against the fact

00:02:21.440 --> 00:02:23.140
that more and more people

00:02:23.140 --> 00:02:25.830
are aware that they are
in danger of losing some

00:02:25.830 --> 00:02:27.400
of their democratic freedoms

00:02:27.400 --> 00:02:29.570
and they're not prepared
to take that lying down.

00:02:29.570 --> 00:02:30.750
They're getting out there,

00:02:30.750 --> 00:02:33.520
they're voting more,
they're organizing online

00:02:33.520 --> 00:02:36.070
and sometimes they're
demonstrating in the streets.

00:02:40.500 --> 00:02:42.810
The biggest election in 2019

00:02:42.810 --> 00:02:44.480
will be in India.

00:02:44.480 --> 00:02:46.730
As always it will be the biggest election

00:02:46.730 --> 00:02:48.650
held anywhere ever.

00:02:48.650 --> 00:02:51.297
The fact that we don't
know who's going to win

00:02:51.297 --> 00:02:53.200
maybe the incumbent party,

00:02:53.200 --> 00:02:54.620
maybe the opposition,

00:02:54.620 --> 00:02:57.680
gives you a sense that it
really will represent roughly

00:02:57.680 --> 00:02:59.500
the will of a billion people.

00:02:59.500 --> 00:03:02.320
Another big one to watch is Nigeria.

00:03:02.320 --> 00:03:04.370
That will be incredibly corrupt

00:03:04.370 --> 00:03:06.430
and quite a few people will get killed

00:03:06.430 --> 00:03:07.460
but it's worth remembering

00:03:07.460 --> 00:03:09.050
that only a couple of decades ago,

00:03:09.050 --> 00:03:10.960
Nigeria was a dictatorship,

00:03:10.960 --> 00:03:12.460
that's not true anymore

00:03:12.460 --> 00:03:14.380
and despite the absence of a dictator,

00:03:14.380 --> 00:03:17.560
Nigeria has held together
despite all predictions.

00:03:17.560 --> 00:03:19.800
It's another fine example, in fact,

00:03:19.800 --> 00:03:22.140
of how democracy does have the ability

00:03:22.140 --> 00:03:24.350
to hold disparate countries together

00:03:24.350 --> 00:03:27.550
because it reflects the
will of the actual voters.

00:03:27.550 --> 00:03:29.480
And a final big election to watch

00:03:29.480 --> 00:03:31.450
is for the European Parliament.

00:03:31.450 --> 00:03:33.740
And here we don't even
know which countries

00:03:33.740 --> 00:03:34.810
are gonna participate,

00:03:34.810 --> 00:03:36.089
so we don't know whether
Britain's gonna be part

00:03:36.089 --> 00:03:37.740
of it or not.

00:03:37.740 --> 00:03:39.634
So, all eyes are gonna be watching,

00:03:39.634 --> 00:03:42.400
will the European Union hold together,

00:03:42.400 --> 00:03:43.510
will the rise of the populists

00:03:43.510 --> 00:03:46.108
and the nationalists continue?

00:03:46.108 --> 00:03:49.314
And my guess is that
actually they've peaked

00:03:49.314 --> 00:03:51.564
and this could be the
start of their retreat.

